Q3. Selenium IDE Automation

Why Search and Filter Testing is a Good Candidate for Automation

Search and Filter functionality is a good candidate for Selenium IDE automation because:

1. Repeated Testing: The same search and filter test cases are executed in every sprint. Automation helps avoid repeating the same manual steps.

2. Time Saving: Manual regression testing takes 4 hours per cycle and runs twice per sprint. Automation can reduce the time required for repeated test execution.

3. Regression Testing: Automated test cases can be reused after every new release to check whether existing search and filter functionality is still working correctly.

Two Limitations of Selenium IDE

1. Limited Customization: Selenium IDE is mainly record-and-playback based. It is less flexible for complex test scenarios and advanced programming logic.

2. Dynamic Applications: Handling complex dynamic elements and advanced synchronization can be difficult compared to Selenium WebDriver.

Conclusion

Selenium IDE is useful for automating repeated and simple regression test cases. However, complex testing scenarios may require more advanced automation tools.
